// The whole-robot posture moves: a robot that can plan and execute a motion
// bringing every limb to a named posture. Two postures cover the operating
// loop:
// - home: the rest posture, the robot's natural pose to start from and power
//   down at. For an arm, low and close to the robot's body.
// - ready: the working posture, out in the robot's main workspace and poised
//   to take commands. For an arm, raised out in front.
// The exact joint values behind each name are the implementer's business.
// Distinct from the streamed setpoints on the *_link pairings: these are
// discrete planned moves with a result.
//
// move_to_ready and move_to_home have the mark `moves_robot`: each MCP
// server, `peppy node call` and each lease holder asks the daemon
// (`robot_leases.check_move`) whether it may move the robot before it calls
// one of them.
//
// A posture goal is refused with `leader_streaming` while a leader streams
// a limb of the robot, and with `precondition_failed` while a limb executes
// another move. A leader is a robot commander, such as a leader arm or the
// browser panel, or the headset. A posture move fails with `unreachable`
// when no plan brings an arm to the posture, with `resource_unavailable`
// when a limb stops answering, and with `attempt_failed` when it cannot go
// on for another reason. A failed goal gives no result. A cancelled goal,
// whether its caller or the stop of limb_motion cancelled it, gives the
// reason of the cancel and its result.
//
// Pose rule for the results: a result reports where each arm ended, as
// limb_state reports it, or no pose:
// - Each pose is the grasp-point pose of an arm in the robot frame. The
//   header of limb_state defines the grasp point, the robot frame and the
//   slicing of the arrays.
// - The implementer measures the pose of every arm when the goal completes
//   or ends cancelled, after the moves of all its arms ended.
// - When an arm has no fresh measured pose then, the three arrays are
//   empty: the implementer never measured the joints of that arm, or their
//   last measurement is stale.
// - After a cancel or a stop, an arm that was still moving can come to
//   rest away from the reported pose.
{
  peppy_schema: "contract/v1",
  manifest: {
    name: "postures",
    tag: "v1",
  },
  failure_kinds: {
    unreachable: "No plan to the target",
    leader_streaming: "A leader streams a limb of the goal",
  },
  interfaces: {
    actions: [
      {
        name: "move_to_ready",
        goal_service: {
          request_message_format: {
            // Requested move duration (s), up to 60; floored at the
            // implementer's velocity-limit duration. 0 = fastest.
            duration_s: "f64",
          },
        },
        result_service: {
          response_message_format: {
            // The implementer's arm names (e.g. "left_arm") in its fixed
            // order, or none, per the header's pose rule.
            arm_names: { $type: "array", $items: "string" },
            // Measured grasp-point positions (m), per the header's pose rule.
            positions: { $type: "array", $items: "f64" },
            // Measured grasp-point orientations, per the header's pose rule.
            orientations: { $type: "array", $items: "f64" },
          },
        },
        failure_kinds: ["unreachable", "leader_streaming"],
        marks: ["moves_robot"],
      },
      {
        name: "move_to_home",
        goal_service: {
          request_message_format: {
            // Requested move duration (s), up to 60; floored at the
            // implementer's velocity-limit duration. 0 = fastest.
            duration_s: "f64",
          },
        },
        result_service: {
          response_message_format: {
            // The implementer's arm names (e.g. "left_arm") in its fixed
            // order, or none, per the header's pose rule.
            arm_names: { $type: "array", $items: "string" },
            // Measured grasp-point positions (m), per the header's pose rule.
            positions: { $type: "array", $items: "f64" },
            // Measured grasp-point orientations, per the header's pose rule.
            orientations: { $type: "array", $items: "f64" },
          },
        },
        failure_kinds: ["unreachable", "leader_streaming"],
        marks: ["moves_robot"],
      },
    ],
  },
}
